From 043a0a098fc74b76d91302f1d48a6cf2a820abb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:05:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Control Strip: collapsed and expanded rows

With ControlStripKeys in the config the media row becomes the expanded
Control Strip, and a second row shows AppLayerKeys on the left and the
collapsed strip (ControlStripKeys) at the right end, as on macOS. Buttons
with Command = "Expand" / "Collapse" switch between the two on release,
while the finger is still on the button. ControlStripDefault sets the state
at start and after each /run/tiny-dfr/layer change. Without ControlStripKeys
both rows are the media row and nothing changes.

The rows now have fixed places (F-keys, collapsed, expanded) and the one
shown follows from the base (MediaLayerDefault, /run/tiny-dfr/layer, double
Fn), Fn held and the strip state, instead of swapping two layers.

Also: a finished touch is forgotten (a later touch that missed every button
could move the old one), and a moving touch is checked against the row it
started on.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
